   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Questions in indirect speech",
     "texto": [
      "Yes/no questions take **ob**: **Er fragte, ob wir kommen** (he asked whether we were coming). Questions with a pronoun or adverb (wann, wo, wer) keep the question word: **Er fragte, wann wir kommen** (he asked when we were coming). In both cases the verb goes at the end."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Requests and orders",
     "texto": [
      "Requests are reported with **bitten** + **zu** + infinitive: **Er bat mich, leise zu sein** (he asked me to be quiet). Orders, with **sollen**: **Sie sagte, ich solle warten** (she said I should wait).",
      "Watch out for the false friend: **bitten** means \"to ask\" in the sense of asking a favour, not \"to order\" in a restaurant (that's «bestellen»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
